IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`
IMPORT `coa26-ch2b`

-- coa26-ch2a.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 42, Chapter 2 (Individuals and firms), ss 1212 to 1216:
-- eligibility for appointment, the effect of ineligibility (duties and offences), the independence requirement,
-- the effect of lack of independence, and the effect of the appointment of a partnership.
-- Lines 17030-17114 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. It imports coa26-ch2b.l4 (ss 1217-1222) for s 1217(2) and s 1217(4).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa26-ch1.l4 (MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, each
-- such branch with a FALSE-kind comment; NOTHING otherwise, each branch with a NOTHING-kind comment).
-- The duties of ss 1213(2) and 1215(1) are encoded twice: as a regulative rule (traced) and as a decision function
-- (asserted), because the stable binary cannot assert a DEONTIC outcome. Time in a trace is counted in days; "immediately" is WITHIN 0.

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Individuals and firms`

§§§ `Eligibility for appointment (s 1212)`

-- src:17032 | (1) An individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor if the individual or firm—
-- src:17033 | (a) is a member of a recognised supervisory body, and
-- src:17034 | (b) is eligible for appointment under the rules of that body.
@ref s 1212(1) Individuals and firms: eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor (src:17032-17034)
GIVEN `the individual or firm is subject to the rules of the supervisory body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 10 recognised supervisory bodies: the body is a recognised supervisory body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual or firm is eligible for appointment under the rules of that body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1212(1) the individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` MEANS
    -- (a) is a member of a recognised supervisory body: a member is a person subject to its rules (s 1217(2)); recognition is s 1217(4)
    -- (b) is eligible for appointment under the rules of that body
    -- a failed "if" is read as the text's no (a lawyer's reading, see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual or firm is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor if the individual or firm— (a) is a member of a recognised supervisory body, and (b) is eligible for appointment under the rules of that body"
    `coa26 support both answers` `limb (a)` `limb (b)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            `coa26 support both answers` `a member of the body` `a recognised body`
        `a member of the body` MEANS
            `s 1217(2) the person is a member of the supervisory body` `the individual or firm is subject to the rules of the supervisory body in seeking appointment or acting as a statutory auditor`
        `a recognised body` MEANS
            `s 1217(4) the supervisory body is a recognised supervisory body for the purposes of Part 42` `sch 10 recognised supervisory bodies: the body is a recognised supervisory body`
        `limb (b)` MEANS JUST `the individual or firm is eligible for appointment under the rules of that body`

-- src:17035 | (2) In the cases to which section 1222 applies (individuals retaining only 1967 Act authorisation) a person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is restricted as mentioned in that section.
@ref s 1212(2) Individuals retaining only 1967 Act authorisation (src:17035)
GIVEN `section 1222 applies to the person (individuals retaining only 1967 Act authorisation)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1212(2) the person's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor is restricted as mentioned in section 1222` MEANS
    IF `section 1222 applies to the person (individuals retaining only 1967 Act authorisation)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the cases to which section 1222 applies"

§§§ `Effect of ineligibility (s 1213)`

-- src:17037 | (1) No person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person if he is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1213(1) No person may act as statutory auditor if ineligible (src:17037)
GIVEN `the person is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1213(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person` MEANS
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the person is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person if he is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text forbids acting while ineligible; it does not itself give a permission to anyone else (see s 1214)

-- src:17037 | (1) No person may act as statutory auditor of an audited person if he is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1213(1) The prohibition, as a regulative rule (src:17037)
`s 1213(1) acts as statutory auditor of the audited person` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "acts as statutory auditor of the audited person"

GIVEN `the person is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1213(1) the prohibition on acting while ineligible` MEANS
    IF `the person is ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
    THEN PARTY Auditor
         SHANT `s 1213(1) acts as statutory auditor of the audited person`
         LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "acted as statutory auditor of an audited person while ineligible for appointment"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:17038 | (2) If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, he must immediately—
-- src:17039 | (a) resign his office (with immediate effect), and
-- src:17040 | (b) give notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible for appointment.
@ref s 1213(2) Duty to resign and give notice on becoming ineligible (src:17038-17040)
GIVEN `the person is a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at a time during his term of office` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1213(2) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes ineligible"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person becomes ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor at a time during his term of office`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, he must immediately" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person has become ineligible is answered by section 1212 and Schedule 10

`s 1213(2)(a) resigns his office with immediate effect` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "resigns his office with immediate effect"
`s 1213(2)(b) gives notice in writing that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "gives notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible for appointment"

-- src:17038 | (2) If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, he must immediately—
-- src:17039 | (a) resign his office (with immediate effect), and
-- src:17040 | (b) give notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible for appointment.
@ref s 1213(2) The duty as a regulative rule (src:17038-17040)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1213(2) the duty of a statutory auditor who becomes ineligible` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor
    MUST `s 1213(2)(a) resigns his office with immediate effect`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE (
        PARTY Auditor
        MUST `s 1213(2)(b) gives notice in writing that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible`
        WITHIN 0
        LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "did not give notice in writing to the audited person that he had resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "did not resign his office immediately on becoming ineligible"

-- src:17041 | (3) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17042 | (a) he acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1), or
-- src:17043 | (b) he fails to give the notice mentioned in paragraph (b) of subsection (2) in accordance with that subsection.
@ref s 1213(3) Offence (src:17041-17043)
GIVEN `the person acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to give the notice mentioned in subsection (2)(b) in accordance with that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1213(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1)`
        OR `the person fails to give the notice mentioned in subsection (2)(b) in accordance with that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if— (a) he acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1), or (b) he fails to give the notice" (a failed "if", a lawyer's reading)

-- src:17044 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable—
-- src:17045 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:17046 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1213(4) Penalty for an offence under subsection (3) (src:17044-17046)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 1213(4) the penalty for an offence under subsection (3)` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `how the person is convicted`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING -- the subsection names no imprisonment
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `the fine limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING -- none is named in this subsection
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHERE
        `the fine limit` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
            WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `a fine without a stated limit`
            WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1
            WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1
            WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1
            WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1

GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1213(4) the most the person can be fined, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a fine" states no limit, so there is no figure
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST `the statutory maximum, in pounds`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST `the statutory maximum, in pounds`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST `the statutory maximum, in pounds`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST `the statutory maximum, in pounds`

-- src:17047 | (5) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17048 | (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(a) or this subsection, and
-- src:17049 | (b) he continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1) after the conviction.
@ref s 1213(5) Offence of continuing to act after a conviction (src:17047-17049)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(a) or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1) after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1213(5) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(a) or this subsection`
       AND `the person continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1) after the conviction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if— (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(a) or this subsection, and (b) he continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of subsection (1) after the conviction."

-- src:17050 | (6) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17051 | (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(b) or this subsection, and
-- src:17052 | (b) he continues, after the conviction, to fail to give the notice mentioned in subsection (2)(b).
@ref s 1213(6) Offence of continuing to fail to give notice after a conviction (src:17050-17052)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(b) or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the conviction the person continues to fail to give the notice mentioned in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1213(6) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(b) or this subsection`
       AND `after the conviction the person continues to fail to give the notice mentioned in subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if— (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (3)(b) or this subsection, and (b) he continues, after the conviction, to fail to give the notice"

-- The fine of subsections (7) in s 1213 and (6) in s 1215 is "one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the
-- amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences for each day on which the act or the failure continues": the
-- rendering shows both the earlier and the substituted words. The substituted words (the second) are encoded; see the fork register.
DECLARE `s 1213(7) fine for continuing` IS ONE OF
    `s 1213(7) a fine without a stated limit`
    `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` HAS `s 1213(7) pounds for each day` IS A NUMBER

-- src:17053 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (5) or (6) is liable—
-- src:17054 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:17055 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences for each day on which the act or the failure continues.
@ref s 1213(7) Penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6) (src:17053-17055)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 1213(7) fine for continuing`
`s 1213(7) the penalty for an offence under subsection (5) or (6)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `s 1213(7) a fine without a stated limit`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHERE
        `the greater of £5,000 or level 4` MEANS
            IF `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds` GREATER THAN 5000
            THEN `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds`
            ELSE 5000
        `a fine for each day` MEANS
            `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` (`the greater of £5,000 or level 4` DIVIDED BY 10)

-- src:17056 | (8) In proceedings against a person for an offence under this section it is a defence for him to show that he did not know and had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1213(8) Defence (src:17056)
GIVEN `the person shows that he did not know that he was, or had become, ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that he had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1213(8) the defence is made out` MEANS
    IF     `the person shows that he did not know that he was, or had become, ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
       AND `the person shows that he had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for him to show that he did not know and had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, ineligible": this section gives no defence on these facts (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

§§ `Independence requirement`

§§§ `s 1214 Independence requirement`

-- src:17070 | (5) An auditor of an audited person is not to be regarded as an officer or employee of the person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3).
@ref s 1214(5) An auditor is not an officer or employee of the audited person (src:17070)
GIVEN `the position is that of an auditor of the audited person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the audited person, or an employee of it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1214(5) the position counts as that of an officer or employee of the audited person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)` MEANS
    IF `the position is that of an auditor of the audited person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor of an audited person is not to be regarded as an officer or employee of the person for the purposes of subsections (2) and (3)."
    ELSE `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the audited person, or an employee of it`

-- src:17060 | (2) This subsection applies if the person is—
-- src:17061 | (a) an officer or employee of the audited person, or
-- src:17062 | (b) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner.
@ref s 1214(2) The audited person's own officers, employees and partners (src:17060-17062)
GIVEN `the person holds a position counting as that of an officer or employee of the audited person (see subsection (5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1214(2) this subsection applies to the person` MEANS
    -- "This subsection applies if the person is (a) ... or (b) ...": JUST TRUE when a limb holds; JUST FALSE when none holds (a failed "if");
    -- NOTHING when limb (a) rests on an answer that is not known and no other limb holds.
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies if the person is— (a) an officer or employee of the audited person, or (b) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner."
    `coa26 support any of the answers` `the limbs`
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS
            LIST `the person holds a position counting as that of an officer or employee of the audited person (see subsection (5))`
               , JUST `the person is a partner or employee of such a person`
               , JUST `the person is a partnership of which such a person is a partner`

-- src:17063 | (3) This subsection applies if the person is—
-- src:17064 | (a) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the audited person, or
-- src:17065 | (b) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner.
@ref s 1214(3) The officers, employees and partners of an associated undertaking (src:17063-17065)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the person is an officer of an associated undertaking of the audited person, or an employee of it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1214(3) this subsection applies to the person` MEANS
    -- Subsection (5) takes an auditor of the audited person out of "officer or employee of the person"; the associated
    -- undertaking is a different person, so subsection (5) is not applied here (see the fork register).
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies if the person is— (a) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the audited person, or (b) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner."
    `coa26 support any of the answers` `the limbs`
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS
            LIST `s 1173(1) the person is an officer of an associated undertaking of the audited person, or an employee of it`
               , JUST `the person is a partner or employee of such a person`
               , JUST `the person is a partnership of which such a person is a partner`

-- src:17066 | (4) This subsection applies if there exists, between—
-- src:17067 | (a) the person or an associate of his, and
-- src:17068 | (b) the audited person or an associated undertaking of the audited person,
-- src:17069 | a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1214(4) A connection specified by regulations (src:17066-17069)
GIVEN `a connection exists between the person or an associate of his and the audited person or an associated undertaking of the audited person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the connection is of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State under subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1214(4) this subsection applies to the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `a connection exists between the person or an associate of his and the audited person or an associated undertaking of the audited person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies if there exists, between— (a) the person or an associate of his, and (b) the audited person or an associated undertaking of the audited person, a connection"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the connection is of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State under subsection (4)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations are not among the sources, so the descriptions they specify are an input

-- src:17071 | (6) In this section “associated undertaking”, in relation to an audited person, means—
-- src:17072 | (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the audited person, or
-- src:17073 | (b) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the audited person.
@ref s 1214(6) "associated undertaking" (src:17071-17073)
GIVEN `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a parent undertaking of the audited person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the audited person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the audited person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1214(6) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the audited person` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “associated undertaking”, in relation to an audited person, means—" (every limb JUST FALSE)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "parent undertaking" and "subsidiary undertaking" are s 1162 and Schedule 7 (the keel and coa29)
    `coa26 support any of the answers` `the limbs`
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS
            LIST `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a parent undertaking of the audited person`
               , `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the audited person`
               , `s 1162(2) the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the audited person`

-- src:17059 | (1) A person may not act as statutory auditor of an audited person if one or more of subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to him.
@ref s 1214(1) A person may not act as statutory auditor if (2), (3) or (4) applies (src:17059)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (3) applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1214(1) the person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` MEANS
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` (`coa26 support any of the answers` `the three subsections`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not act as statutory auditor of an audited person if one or more of subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to him."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection forbids acting while one of them applies; it grants no permission
    WHERE
        `the three subsections` MEANS
            LIST `subsection (2) applies to the person`, `subsection (3) applies to the person`, `subsection (4) applies to the person`

-- src:17059 | (1) A person may not act as statutory auditor of an audited person if one or more of subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to him.
@ref s 1214(1) The prohibition, as a regulative rule (src:17059)
`s 1214(1) acts as statutory auditor of the audited person` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "acts as statutory auditor of the audited person"

GIVEN `one or more of subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1214(1) the prohibition on acting without independence` MEANS
    IF `one or more of subsections (2), (3) and (4) apply to the person`
    THEN PARTY Auditor
         SHANT `s 1214(1) acts as statutory auditor of the audited person`
         LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "acted as statutory auditor of an audited person to whom subsection (2), (3) or (4) of section 1214 applied"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 1214(7) (regulations under subsection (4) are subject to negative resolution procedure) is machinery (coverage: inert, reason 2).

§§ `Effect of lack of independence`

§§§ `s 1215 Effect of lack of independence`

-- src:17076 | (1) If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes prohibited from acting by section 1214(1), he must immediately—
-- src:17077 | (a) resign his office (with immediate effect), and
-- src:17078 | (b) give notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his lack of independence.
@ref s 1215(1) Duty to resign and give notice on becoming prohibited from acting (src:17076-17078)
GIVEN `the person is a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at a time during his term of office the person becomes prohibited from acting by section 1214(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1215(1) the statutory auditor must immediately resign and give notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes prohibited from acting by section 1214(1), he must immediately"
    ELSE CONSIDER `at a time during his term of office the person becomes prohibited from acting by section 1214(1)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes prohibited from acting by section 1214(1), he must immediately" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 1214(1) prohibits the person is answered by section 1214

`s 1215(1)(a) resigns his office with immediate effect` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "resigns his office with immediate effect"
`s 1215(1)(b) gives notice in writing that he has resigned by reason of his lack of independence` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "gives notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his lack of independence"

-- src:17076 | (1) If at any time during his term of office a statutory auditor becomes prohibited from acting by section 1214(1), he must immediately—
-- src:17077 | (a) resign his office (with immediate effect), and
-- src:17078 | (b) give notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his lack of independence.
@ref s 1215(1) The duty as a regulative rule (src:17076-17078)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1215(1) the duty of a statutory auditor who becomes prohibited from acting` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor
    MUST `s 1215(1)(a) resigns his office with immediate effect`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE (
        PARTY Auditor
        MUST `s 1215(1)(b) gives notice in writing that he has resigned by reason of his lack of independence`
        WITHIN 0
        LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "did not give notice in writing to the audited person that he had resigned by reason of his lack of independence"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "did not resign his office immediately on becoming prohibited from acting by section 1214(1)"

-- src:17079 | (2) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17080 | (a) he acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1), or
-- src:17081 | (b) he fails to give the notice mentioned in paragraph (b) of subsection (1) in accordance with that subsection.
@ref s 1215(2) Offence (src:17079-17081)
GIVEN `the person acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to give the notice mentioned in paragraph (b) of subsection (1) in accordance with that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1215(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1)`
        OR `the person fails to give the notice mentioned in paragraph (b) of subsection (1) in accordance with that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if— (a) he acts as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1), or (b) he fails to give the notice" (a failed "if", a lawyer's reading)

-- src:17082 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (2) is liable—
-- src:17083 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:17084 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1215(3) Penalty for an offence under subsection (2) (src:17082-17084)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 1215(3) the penalty for an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `how the person is convicted`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING -- the subsection names no imprisonment
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `the fine limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING -- none is named in this subsection
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHERE
        `the fine limit` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
            WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `a fine without a stated limit`
            WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1
            WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1
            WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1
            WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1

-- src:17085 | (4) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17086 | (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(a) or this subsection, and
-- src:17087 | (b) he continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1) after the conviction.
@ref s 1215(4) Offence of continuing to act after a conviction (src:17085-17087)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(a) or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1) after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1215(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(a) or this subsection`
       AND `the person continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1) after the conviction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if— (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(a) or this subsection, and (b) he continues to act as a statutory auditor in contravention of section 1214(1) after the conviction."

-- src:17088 | (5) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17089 | (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(b) or this subsection, and
-- src:17090 | (b) after the conviction, he continues to fail to give the notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b).
@ref s 1215(5) Offence of continuing to fail to give notice after a conviction (src:17088-17090)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(b) or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the conviction the person continues to fail to give the notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1215(5) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(b) or this subsection`
       AND `after the conviction the person continues to fail to give the notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if— (a) he has been convicted of an offence under subsection (2)(b) or this subsection, and (b) after the conviction, he continues to fail to give the notice"

-- src:17091 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4) or (5) is liable—
-- src:17092 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:17093 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences for each day on which the act or the failure continues.
@ref s 1215(6) Penalty for an offence under subsection (4) or (5) (src:17091-17093)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 1213(7) fine for continuing`
`s 1215(6) the penalty for an offence under subsection (4) or (5)` MEANS
    -- the same words as s 1213(7); the type is declared at s 1213(7)
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `s 1213(7) a fine without a stated limit`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN `a fine for each day`
    WHERE
        `the greater of £5,000 or level 4` MEANS
            IF `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds` GREATER THAN 5000
            THEN `the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences, in pounds`
            ELSE 5000
        `a fine for each day` MEANS
            `s 1213(7) a fine not exceeding a sum for each day on which the act or the failure continues` (`the greater of £5,000 or level 4` DIVIDED BY 10)

-- src:17094 | (7) In proceedings against a person for an offence under this section it is a defence for him to show that he did not know and had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, prohibited from acting as statutory auditor of the audited person by section 1214(1).
@ref s 1215(7) Defence (src:17094)
GIVEN `the person shows that he did not know that he was, or had become, prohibited from acting as statutory auditor of the audited person by section 1214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that he had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, prohibited from acting as statutory auditor of the audited person by section 1214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1215(7) the defence is made out` MEANS
    IF     `the person shows that he did not know that he was, or had become, prohibited from acting as statutory auditor of the audited person by section 1214(1)`
       AND `the person shows that he had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, prohibited from acting as statutory auditor of the audited person by section 1214(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for him to show that he did not know and had no reason to believe that he was, or had become, prohibited": this section gives no defence on these facts (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

§§ `Effect of appointment of a partnership`

§§§ `s 1216 Effect of appointment of a partnership`

-- src:17097 | (1) This section applies where a partnership constituted under the law of—
-- src:17098 | (a) England and Wales,
-- src:17099 | (b) Northern Ireland, or
-- src:17100 | (c) any other country or territory in which a partnership is not a legal person,
-- src:17101 | is by virtue of this Chapter appointed as statutory auditor of an audited person.
@ref s 1216(1) Where the section applies (src:17097-17101)
GIVEN `the partnership is constituted under the law of England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partnership is constituted under the law of Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partnership is constituted under the law of another country or territory in which a partnership is not a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partnership is by virtue of Chapter 2 appointed as statutory auditor of an audited person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF     `the partnership is by virtue of Chapter 2 appointed as statutory auditor of an audited person`
       AND (   `the partnership is constituted under the law of England and Wales`
            OR `the partnership is constituted under the law of Northern Ireland`
            OR `the partnership is constituted under the law of another country or territory in which a partnership is not a legal person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a partnership constituted under the law of— (a) England and Wales, (b) Northern Ireland, or (c) any other country or territory in which a partnership is not a legal person, is by virtue of this Chapter appointed as statutory auditor of an audited person."

-- src:17102 | (2) Unless a contrary intention appears, the appointment is an appointment of the partnership as such and not of the partners.
@ref s 1216(2) The appointment is of the partnership as such (src:17102)
GIVEN `section 1216(1) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(2) the appointment is an appointment of the partnership as such and not of the partners` MEANS
    CONSIDER `section 1216(1) applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where" the partnership is appointed and constituted as stated in subsection (1)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the partnership is within subsection (1) is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a contrary intention appears`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a contrary intention appears, the appointment is an appointment of the partnership as such and not of the partners." (an "unless" once met: decided case by case, see the fork register)
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:17107 | (a) a partnership is to be regarded as succeeding to the practice of another partnership only if the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership, and
@ref s 1216(4)(a) A partnership succeeds only if its members are substantially the same (src:17107)
GIVEN `the successor is a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(4)(a) the partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` MEANS
    IF `the successor is a partnership` AND (NOT `the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a partnership is to be regarded as succeeding to the practice of another partnership only if the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" states a necessary condition; whether the successor in fact succeeds is a fact

-- src:17108 | (b) a partnership or other person is to be regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership only if it or he succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership.
@ref s 1216(4)(b) A partnership or other person succeeds only if it takes the whole or substantially the whole of the business (src:17108)
GIVEN `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(4)(b) the partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` MEANS
    IF NOT `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a partnership or other person is to be regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership only if it or he succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" states a necessary condition; whether the successor in fact succeeds is a fact

-- src:17112 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a partnership or other person is “appropriate” if it or he—
-- src:17113 | (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of this Chapter, and
-- src:17114 | (b) is not prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of the audited person.
@ref s 1216(6) "appropriate" (src:17112-17114)
GIVEN `s 1212(1) the partnership or other person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1214(1) the partnership or other person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(6) the partnership or other person is appropriate` MEANS
    -- "is not prohibited by section 1214(1)": prohibited means the answer to s 1214(1) is JUST FALSE; NOTHING there is not a prohibition.
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a partnership or other person is “appropriate” if it or he— (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of this Chapter, and (b) is not prohibited by section 1214(1)"
    `coa26 support both answers` `s 1212(1) the partnership or other person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2` `not prohibited`
    WHERE
        `not prohibited` MEANS
            IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` `s 1214(1) the partnership or other person may act as statutory auditor of the audited person`
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:17103 | (3) Where the partnership ceases, the appointment is to be treated as extending to—
-- src:17104 | (a) any appropriate partnership which succeeds to the practice of that partnership, or
-- src:17105 | (b) any other appropriate person who succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership.
@ref s 1216(3) Where the partnership ceases (src:17103-17105)
GIVEN `the partnership ceases` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the successor is an appropriate partnership which in fact succeeds to the practice of that partnership` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the successor is another appropriate person who in fact succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1216(4)(a) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1216(4)(b) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(3) the appointment is treated as extending to the successor` MEANS
    -- "Where the partnership ceases": JUST FALSE when it has not. Subsection (4) limits "succeeds": a JUST FALSE from (4)(a) or (4)(b) is no succession.
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the partnership ceases` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the partnership ceases, the appointment is to be treated as extending to"
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` `s 1216(4)(a) answer` OR `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` `s 1216(4)(b) answer`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if" in subsection (4)(a) and (b): the successor is not regarded as succeeding to the practice
        OTHERWISE `coa26 support either answer` `the successor is an appropriate partnership which in fact succeeds to the practice of that partnership` `the successor is another appropriate person who in fact succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership`

-- src:17109 | (5) Where the partnership ceases and the appointment is not treated under subsection (3) as extending to any partnership or other person, the appointment may with the consent of the audited person be treated as extending to an appropriate partnership, or other appropriate person, who succeeds to—
-- src:17110 | (a) the business of the former partnership, or
-- src:17111 | (b) such part of it as is agreed by the audited person is to be treated as comprising the appointment.
@ref s 1216(5) Extension with the consent of the audited person (src:17109-17111)
GIVEN `the partnership ceases` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is treated under subsection (3) as extending to a partnership or other person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the audited person consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the successor is an appropriate partnership or other appropriate person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the successor succeeds to the business of the former partnership, or to such part of it as is agreed by the audited person is to be treated as comprising the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1216(5) the appointment may be treated as extending to the successor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the partnership ceases` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the partnership ceases and the appointment is not treated under subsection (3) as extending to any partnership or other person"
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the appointment is treated under subsection (3) as extending to a partnership or other person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the appointment is not treated under subsection (3) as extending to any partnership or other person"
        IF NOT `the audited person consents` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may with the consent of the audited person"
        IF NOT `the successor succeeds to the business of the former partnership, or to such part of it as is agreed by the audited person is to be treated as comprising the appointment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who succeeds to— (a) the business of the former partnership, or (b) such part of it as is agreed"
        OTHERWISE `the successor is an appropriate partnership or other appropriate person`
